* AD8237 Instrumentation Amplifier Circuit
.lib AD8237.lib

* Power Supplies (Single 5V supply)
VCC VCC 0 5V
VEE VEE 0 0V

* Reference voltage at mid-supply
VREF REF 0 2.5V

* Inverting input biased at mid-supply
VINN INN 0 2.5V

* Primary input: 20 mV amplitude sine at 1 kHz, biased at mid-supply
* This creates a 20 mV amplitude differential signal between IN and INN
VIN IN 0 SINE(2.5 20m 1k)

* Gain Setting Resistors
* AD8237 uses indirect current mode architecture where G = 1 + R2/R1
* For G = 10 V/V, R2/R1 = 9
R1 FB REF 1k
R2 FB OUT 9k

* Light load resistor
RL OUT REF 100k

* AD8237 Instance
* Standard LTspice subcircuit pin order for AD8237 matches the 8-lead physical package:
* 1: BW (Bandwidth, tied to VCC for high BW mode)
* 2: -IN (Inverting Input)
* 3: +IN (Non-Inverting Input)
* 4: -VS (Negative Supply)
* 5: REF (Reference)
* 6: FB (Feedback)
* 7: OUT (Output)
* 8: +VS (Positive Supply)
X1 VCC INN IN VEE REF FB OUT VCC AD8237

* Analysis Directives
* Run transient analysis for 5ms, saving data from 2ms to 5ms to allow settling
.tran 0 5m 2m

* Measure peak-to-peak voltages to calculate AC gain
.measure tran in_pp PP V(IN)
.measure tran out_pp PP V(OUT)
.measure tran gain param out_pp/in_pp
.measure tran gain_db param 20*log10(gain)

.end
